claude: true
prompt: >
  You are working on ansill, the Perl implementation of the ANSILL layout
  language. Read .claude/rules/ansill-rules.md, then pick the
  highest-priority actionable ticket from the karr board (`karr board`), claim
  it, and complete it via the ansill-worker agent. The compiler runs five
  stages — parse, resolve, render, validate, emit — and the language
  definition lives in spec/ANSILL.md. Verify with `prove -l t/`; the `-l` is
  mandatory, without it the installed release is loaded instead of lib/.
  dist.ini is the build truth; cpanfile is generated from it. Never run `dzil
  release`, never tag, never push, never upload to CPAN.
